prompt_template:
Create a premium footwear process board.
{STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Process and subject: {SUBJECT}
Material setting, panels and palette: {SCENE}
Tiny stage labels only: {MAIN_TEXT}. Keep step numbers and short labels hairline-small and aligned to panel edges. No title, slogan, or large typography.
Process direction: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Show three or four ordered frames that make the start state, physical transformation and result immediately understandable. Use consistent shoe angles where useful, accurate cross-sections, macro material texture, and one restrained connector between stages. The footwear is an original unbranded design: pearl-bone knit upper, open heel cage, brushed-titanium floating arch bridge, a continuous smoked-ceramic rocker with three long channels, and a smooth integrated forefoot. It must not resemble the source shoe or use separate rounded pods.
Premium tactile photography, deliberate negative space, disciplined panel gutters, warm bone and obsidian with brushed-metal detail and tiny glacial-cyan process marks. The process itself is the visual hero; keep human presence partial and secondary. Recompose explicitly for the requested aspect ratio. Exclude: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}.
